 1. Enter your Paladin + Cleric loadout. A third class is optional; this profile does not depend on one.
 2. Choose your character and current level above. Set the starting level once; future level-up log messages update it while this helper runs.
 3. Stand somewhere safe, out of combat. Focus EverQuest and press F6. Preparation exports your learned spellbook and memorizes ONLY spells you own and can use at your selected level. Each gem waits for EverQuest's own "finished memorizing" message (about 2 seconds for a gem that already holds the spell), so /log must be on. F9 cancels.
-4. Press F8 to turn combat on, heal low HP, and maintain prepared buffs even with no enemy selected. Repeated F8 presses leave it on. It checks for the enemy you select, fights it, then waits for your next selection after the kill. F9 turns combat off. F7 is a single on/off toggle (on like F8, off like F9) for controllers that map a button to F7; the helper consumes F7 so EQ's own Target Nearest PC does not also fire. F8 combat never selects, pulls or moves; only the F11 autopilot does.
-5. Optional: at full health, click Calibrate HP and select just the inside of your red HP gauge. Automatic healing requires this reading. F10 requests your fast heal even without calibration.
+4. Press F8 to turn combat on, heal low HP, and maintain prepared buffs even with no enemy selected. Repeated F8 presses leave it on. It checks for the enemy you select, fights it, then waits for your next selection after the kill. F9 turns combat off. F7 is a single on/off toggle (on like F8, off like F9) for controllers that map a button to F7; the helper consumes F7 so EQ's own Target Nearest PC does not also fire. F8 combat never selects, pulls or moves; F11 travel and F12 recording are disabled in this preview. You control melee yourself; F9 stops further helper input but does not turn melee off or cancel a spell already cast.
+5. At full health, click Find / calibrate HP, check the proposed inner red gauge, and Save only when that outline and full HP are correct. Drag a corrected rectangle if needed. Automatic healing requires this reading. F10 requests your fast heal even without calibration.
 6. Optional: calibrate the blue mana bar. Below 25% mana the assistant saves mana for healing; at 35% or less it also skips buffs, stuns and the Smite ability.
 
 IMPORTANT SOLO SETUP
-Use implied healing (Options → Combat) so a heal while targeting your enemy heals its friendly target — normally you while solo tanking. The installer enables this for your existing offline Blizz/Legira character files, with backups. If you use a different character, enable this option there too.
+Use implied healing (Options → Combat) so a heal while targeting your enemy heals its friendly target — normally you while solo tanking. The helper does not change this game setting; check it yourself for the character you play.
+If a command is interrupted, press F9, close its game chat draft yourself, then click Chat recovery and confirm it is closed. Assist stays OFF until a fresh F8. Cancel leaves the paused state unchanged.
 Keep /log on for automatic level detection and encounter stops. The selected character's log filename must match the character you are playing.
 When you ding, the current fight finishes using its existing bar. Before the next fight, press F6 or the Prepare spell bar button to refresh learned spells and load upgrades. F8 and F7 only switch combat and never start preparation. New spells still need to be scribed normally. Mote upgrades apply in the game as usual.
 Calibrated readings are only valid for the captured resolution and UI layout. An unavailable/invalid HP reading disables automatic healing; F10 remains available.
